	<div class="fsElement fsContent footer-content" id="fsEl_2798" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p><b data-olk-copy-source="MailCompose">Non-Discrimination &amp; Title IX Statement</b></p>

<p>The Holmes County Consolidated School District is committed to providing an equitable, inclusive, and welcoming environment for all students, employees, parents, volunteers, vendors, and members of the public. The District does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, or military status in any of its programs, activities, services, or employment practices.</p>

<p>In accordance with <b>Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972</b>, the Holmes County Consolidated School District does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its education programs or activities. Title IX prohibits discrimination, including sexual harassment, sexual assault, dating violence, domestic violence, and stalking, in educational programs and activities receiving federal financial assistance.</p>

<p>The District is committed to ensuring equal access to educational opportunities and employment and to maintaining an environment free from discrimination and harassment.</p>

<p>To report discrimination, harassment, or a potential <b>Title IX</b> concern, please contact the District&#39;s Title IX Coordinator:</p>

<p><b>Dr. Shem Whigham</b><br />
<b>Title IX Coordinator</b><br />
Email: <a href="mailto:swhigham@holmesccsd.org" id="OWA5fe093e0-612b-ac39-6bcc-d8f7c3a03b3c"><b>swhigham@holmesccsd.org</b></a><br />
Phone: <b>662-834-2175</b></p>


	</div>


